From: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: leave out YUV 4:2:0-only modes by default

A 4K TV behind a USB-C dock typically lists 3840x2160 at 60 Hz as a
YCbCr 4:2:0-only mode, and a compositor picks it as the preferred mode.
Driving it takes the DPU's one CDM block, and dpu_rm hands that block
out per CRTC as each CRTC's atomic_check runs: when the mode moves from
one CRTC to another in a commit (gamescope moving game mode from the
built-in panel to the dock), the new CRTC is checked while the old one
still owns the block, and every commit fails with

  [dpu error]CDM_0 is already allocated
  [dpu error]failed to reserve hw resources: -5

so the TV never gets a picture and the panel has already been given up.
Seen on a Retroid Pocket 6 with the Retroid dock and a 65" 4K TV.

Reject 4:2:0-only modes in mode_valid unless msm.dp_yuv420=1, so the
sink is driven with an RGB mode (4K at 30 Hz, or 1080p) instead. The
CDM ordering is the real bug; this keeps docking working until it is
fixed.

Signed-off-by: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -32,6 +32,16 @@
 module_param(psr_enabled, bool, 0);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(psr_enabled, "enable PSR for eDP and DP displays");
 
+/*
+ * A YUV 4:2:0-only mode needs the DPU's single CDM block, and the resource manager
+ * hands that block to a new CRTC before the CRTC giving it up has been checked, so
+ * moving a 4:2:0 mode between CRTCs (game mode moving to a docked TV) fails every
+ * commit. Leave those modes out unless asked for.
+ */
+static bool dp_yuv420;
+module_param(dp_yuv420, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_yuv420, "Offer YUV 4:2:0-only DisplayPort modes (default: no)");
+
 #define HPD_STRING_SIZE 30
 
 enum {
@@ -789,7 +799,7 @@
 	 * YUV 420 is carried over DP by signalling the colorimetry through a
 	 * VSC SDP, so a 420-only mode cannot be driven without VSC SDP support.
 	 */
-	if (is_yuv_420 && !msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported)
+	if (is_yuv_420 && (!dp_yuv420 || !msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported))
 		return MODE_NO_420;
 
 	link_pclk_khz = is_yuv_420 ? mode_pclk_khz / 2 : mode_pclk_khz;
